  "@type": "urpx:URPXPackage",
  "@id": "sdge:doc-ev-tou-5-2026-04-01",
  "urpx:targetURPXVersion": "https://github.com/urpx-org/urpx/raw/v0.5.1/ontology/urpx-ontology.ttl",
  "urpx:hasRatePlan": {
    "@type": "urpx:RatePlan",
    "@id": "sdge:ev-tou-5",
    "urpx:name": "Schedule EV-TOU-5 Cost-Based Domestic Time-of-Use for Households with Electric Vehicles",
    "urpx:ratePlanUniqueIdentifier": "EV-TOU-5",
    "urpx:initialEffectiveDate": "2020-04-01",
    "urpx:timezoneIdentifier": "America/Los_Angeles",
    "urpx:hasRatePlanVersion": {
      "@type": "urpx:RatePlanVersion",
      "@id": "sdge:ev-tou-5-2026-04-01",
      "urpx:description": "SDG&E's cost-based residential time-of-use rate for households with electric vehicles or natural-gas vehicles. MANDATORY for new solar customers under the Net Billing Tariff (NBT) since 2023 — rapidly growing enrollment as solar adoption accelerates. Estimated ~10% of SDG&E residential = ~140K customers and rising. Three TOU periods (On-Peak / Off-Peak / Super Off-Peak); same TOU windows as TOU-DR1 (4-9pm peak all days; super-off-peak split midnight-6am + 10am-2pm weekdays / continuous midnight-2pm weekends/holidays). Distinguishing structural features vs TOU-DR1: (1) UDC Transmission and Distribution components are TOU-varying — Transmission $0.10067 on/off-peak vs $0.00000 super-off-peak; Distribution $0.21102 vs $0.02601 — designed to incentivize overnight EV charging; (2) UDC TRAC is zero across all periods (vs $0.06762 flat in TOU-DR1); (3) NO Baseline Adjustment Credit (vs $-0.10892 in TOU-DR1); (4) Higher Summer On-Peak EECC ($0.47019 vs $0.34920 — reflects cost-based per-kWh pricing for high-load EV households). Same Base Services Charge $0.79343/day for standard customers; CARE/FERA/DRAH variants modeled as RatePlanModifiers in grid-coordination/urpx-rate-plans#13 secondary epic. Eligibility limited to customers with registered BEV/PHEV/NGV vehicles, OR enrolled in NBT (which makes EV-TOU-5 the otherwise-applicable schedule for new solar customers regardless of EV ownership). HEVs (conventional charge-sustaining hybrids without grid charging) are NOT eligible. Holiday handling: the urpx:HolidayCalendar on this filing carries the eight Time-of-Use Holidays enumerated in SDG&E Electric Rule 1 (Definitions), Sheet 6, Cal. P.U.C. Sheet No. 61672-E. The weekday and the weekend/holiday shapes differ only over 6am-10am, which is Off-Peak on a weekday and Super Off-Peak on a weekend or holiday, so the calendar is applied by excluding holidays from the 6am-10am weekday Off-Peak bracket and adding a 6am-10am weekday Super Off-Peak bracket that admits holidays only. Rule 1 further directs that a Holiday falling on Sunday makes the following Monday a Holiday, with no change for one falling on Saturday. urpx:observanceRule has no value for a Sunday-only shift (its four are actualDateObservance, fridayIfWeekendObservance, mondayIfWeekendObservance and nearestWeekdayObservance), so that direction is carried as urpx:holidayRule text and is not machine-readable: the Monday after a Sunday-falling fixed-date holiday resolves here as an ordinary weekday, first on 2027-07-05.",
      "urpx:effectiveDateTime": "2026-04-01T00:00:00",
      "urpx:minimumTenure": "P12M",
      "urpx:changeReason": {
        "@id": "urpx:rateCase"
      },
      "urpx:priceCurrency": "USD",
      "urpx:commodity": {
        "@id": "urpx:electricity"
      },
      "urpx:serviceRole": {
        "@id": "urpx:bundledServiceRole"
      },
      "urpx:customerChoice": {
        "@id": "urpx:voluntaryChoice"
      },
      "urpx:isDefault": false,
      "urpx:hasDataSourceReference": {
        "@type": "urpx:DataSourceReference",
        "urpx:fileName": "SCHEDULE_EV-TOU-5.pdf",
